// Optional command-line deployment of the smart reports Worker, as smart-push-proxy has. The
// dashboard works too (paste cloudflare-worker-smart-reports.js, set RELAY_ORIGIN and the EDGE_KEY
// secret, add the custom domain reports.woowtech.io, and a WAF rate limiting rule for the per-IP
// limit). Use this file when a binding is wanted: the IP_RATE_LIMITER binding below makes the
// Worker apply 10 requests a minute per IP itself (counted per Cloudflare location, no burst
// setting). Such bindings can only be set through wrangler, not in the dashboard.
//
// Do not edit the RELAY_ORIGIN placeholder: pass the run.app URL that
// woowtech-smart-reports-deploy.sh prints with --var (the placeholder is not an https URL, so a
// Worker deployed without it answers 500). Use wrangler 4.149.0, logged in with its own profile,
// XDG_CONFIG_HOME=~/.local/share/woowtech-smart/wrangler-reports, and only the scopes
// account:read user:read workers_scripts:write workers_routes:write zone:read. There is no
// account_id here: set CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID to the account that has the woowtech.io zone. From
// woowtech/ai-content-report-cloudrun, the first time:
//   npx --yes wrangler@4.149.0 secret put EDGE_KEY --config deploy/cloudflare-worker-smart-reports.wrangler.jsonc
//   npx --yes wrangler@4.149.0 deploy --config deploy/cloudflare-worker-smart-reports.wrangler.jsonc --var "RELAY_ORIGIN:<run.app URL>"
// A wrangler deploy replaces the variables set in the dashboard (ALLOWED_ORIGINS among them) with
// the ones here and on the command line; it keeps secrets such as EDGE_KEY. Updating the Worker
// alone, with the checks before and after, is in ../README.md.
// EDGE_KEY is one key. While a rotation leaves "old new" in the Secret Manager secret, give it the
// new key only (the deploy script's rotation steps print how); the pair would make every request 403.
// namespace_id must be an integer, as a string, and unique among rate limiting namespaces in the
// Cloudflare account: smart-push-proxy uses 4101.
{
  "name": "smart-reports-proxy",
  "main": "cloudflare-worker-smart-reports.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  // workers.dev and Preview URLs off, as in the dashboard's Settings > Domains & Routes: they are
  // outside the woowtech.io zone and its per-IP rate limit.
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "reports.woowtech.io", "custom_domain": true }],
  // No Workers Logs and no Logpush: the Worker sees client addresses and request bodies.
  "observability": { "enabled": false },
  "logpush": false,
  "vars": {
    "RELAY_ORIGIN": "set-me:the-run.app-URL-printed-by-woowtech-smart-reports-deploy.sh",
  },
  "ratelimits": [
    {
      "name": "IP_RATE_LIMITER",
      "namespace_id": "4102",
      "simple": { "limit": 10, "period": 60 },
    },
  ],
}
